Secretome Annotations & Per-Gland Mastersheets (Mouse)
Builds a Geneid → secretome/function dictionary and per-gland TPM mastersheets (PAR, SM, SL, LIV, PANC) with:
secreted flag (yes / No_annotation / manual_annotation)
Reference, Function
Mean_TPM, Mean_TPM_Male, Mean_TPM_Fem
Repo layout
secretome_annotation_dictionary.R — builds Geneid_secretome_dictionary.csv/.rds
annotate_each_gland_secreted_non_secreted_mouse.R — creates {GLAND}_mastersheet_TPMs_annotated.csv
mouse_proteome/function_add.csv — edit to set/override Function (and optional Reference)
mouse_proteome/mannual_curation.csv — edit to set secreted = manual_annotation (and optional Reference/Function)
Input TPMs: gene_expression_matrix_C57_CD1_TPMs.csv
Note: known contaminated PAR columns are dropped automatically inside the mastersheet script.
Update workflows
Update Function only
Edit mouse_proteome/function_add.csv (add/modify row for your Geneid; set Function, optional Reference).
Run secretome_annotation_dictionary.R.
Run annotate_each_gland_secreted_non_secreted_mouse.R.
Update secreted / not (manual)
Edit mouse_proteome/mannual_curation.csv (add/modify row; set secreted = manual_annotation; optional Reference/Function).
Run secretome_annotation_dictionary.R.
Run annotate_each_gland_secreted_non_secreted_mouse.R.
Outputs
Dictionary: mouse_proteome/Geneid_secretome_dictionary.csv (+ .rds)
Mastersheets: {PAR,SM,SL,LIV,PANC}_mastersheet_TPMs_annotated.csv
Notes
Sex means are inferred from column names containing -Mal- / -Fem-.
Keep Geneid values consistent with TPM headers.
